			<div class="content" id="post-content-4736690">
									

<p>The premise? Extremely creepy. The journal entries? Well-written. My problems with this lie with the &quot;anomalous&quot; connections in the journals. The dream/vision sequence felt particularly uninspired, and while the City All Of Blood connection was nice, you introduce more and more elements (Algadda, Hanged King, 035) in such a surface-level, referential way that the entire piece becomes unfocused. Goya having a connection to all of these anomalies in a short span of time took me out of the story. The final AWCY? mentioned borders on ridiculous, and felt more forced than anything else in the article.</p>

